00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.950
along with BeyondCorp.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.490
Now, the first thing
is really, when

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:44.990
working in a hybrid
environment, you

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:48.320
need to get your users
to get access to GCP.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.880
And so after you've
created your organization,

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.720
one of the first things to do
is to go and start figuring out

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.790
how to grant your
developers, the rest

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:58.840
the folks that actually need
access to the environment

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.170
permissions.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:02.950
And so to grant access, we use
something called Google Cloud

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:06.640
Identity, which is a Google
service that allows customers

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:10.240
to create and manage
users, as well as groups,

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:13.400
in order to grant them
access to cloud resources.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.390
Now in addition to
granting access to GCP,

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:19.610
Google Cloud Identity is
also a standalone offering.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:22.900
It has IDaaS capabilities
that allows it to do things

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.090
like robust lifecycle
management, device

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:28.060
policies, provisioning of
users across a multitude

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:31.033
of different applications.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:32.700
If your identities
are actually residing

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:35.480
in an on prem, just
like this example shows,

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.090
you can synchronize it using
a tool called Google Cloud

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:41.390
Directory Synchronization,
or GCDS for short.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:44.570
This tool allows you to select
the specific users using

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:46.642
LDAP across either
an LDAP filter

00:02:46.642 --> 00:02:49.100
to select which set of users
you want to bring in or select

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.990
the set of OUs that
you have in order

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:55.020
to pull those identities in.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:59.130
In order to configure single
sign on, you can use SAML,

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.590
either in this case
using an ADFS instance,

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:04.650
or any really federation
token broker that

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.410
allows you to take identities
from your on-prem system,

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.870
present a SAML assertion that
can be used in order to grant

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.170
them single sign on into GCP.

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:16.800
If your company happens to use
